---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="US vs UK Bra Sizes: Key Differences & Conversion | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Learn the key differences between US and UK bra sizing. Understand why UK cup progression (DD, E, F, FF, G) differs from US cup progression after D cup."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/guides/us-vs-uk-bra-sizing"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Guides', url: '/#guides' },
      { label: 'US vs UK Bra Sizing' }
    ]} />

    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Evergreen Guide
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        US vs UK Bra Sizes: Differences & Conversion Guide
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-xs text-mute mb-4">
        <span>By BraSizeChecker Editorial Team</span>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <time datetime="2026-08-24">Updated August 2026</time>
      </div>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Shopping for underwear internationally can be confusing because US and UK sizing standards match up to a D cup, but diverge significantly starting at 5-inch bust differences.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">1. The Cup Progression Divergence</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          US manufacturers use single-letter extensions or multiple D's (`DDD/F`, `G`, `H`, `I`, `J`), whereas British brands use double-letter conventions (`DD`, `E`, `F`, `FF`, `G`, `GG`, `H`, `HH`):
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto -mx-2 px-2 mb-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-body border-collapse min-w-[400px]">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-hairline bg-canvas-soft-2 text-ink">
                <th scope="col" class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold">Bust-Band Difference</th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold">US Cup Progression</th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold">UK Cup Progression</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
              <tr><td class="py-2 px-3">5 inches</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-ink">DD / E</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-primary">DD</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="py-2 px-3">6 inches</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-ink">DDD / F</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-primary">E</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="py-2 px-3">7 inches</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-ink">G</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-primary">F</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="py-2 px-3">8 inches</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-ink">H</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-primary">FF</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="py-2 px-3">9 inches</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-ink">I</td><td class="py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-primary">G</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">2. Converting Your Size Instantly</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Convert your size between American and British standards instantly with our tools:
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/bra-size-converter" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-primary text-white font-bold text-xs rounded-xl hover:bg-primary-hover shadow-2xs">Converter Tool &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/uk-bra-size-guide" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-surface border border-hairline text-ink font-semibold text-xs rounded-xl hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 shadow-2xs">UK Sizing Guide &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
